# Copy to .env.local. Every value here is optional — the app runs without any
# of them, against public mainnet infrastructure.

# Starknet mainnet RPC. Defaults to the public endpoint from the sprint's Day 0
# guide. Set your own (Alchemy, Infura, Lava) for anything beyond a demo:
# public endpoints rate-limit, and receipt polling during a payment is chatty.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_RPC_URL=https://rpc.starknet.lava.build

# Absolute origin used when building shareable links. Set this when the app sits
# behind a custom domain or a proxy that rewrites Host; otherwise forwarded
# headers are used, which is correct on Vercel out of the box.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=https://whisperpay.example

# Durable status store — an Upstash-compatible Redis, over its REST API.
#
# Not optional on serverless, whatever this file's header says. Without it,
# status lives in process memory, and on Vercel the API route and the /s/<id>
# page run as separate functions with separate memory: the route reports a
# payment while the status page still shows it unpaid. Paying itself is
# unaffected either way — a payment link carries the whole request and never
# reads the store.
#
# Provision it from the Vercel Marketplace (Upstash Redis) or at upstash.com.
# Whichever pair your host injects is read; you don't need both, and neither
# name is preferred. A redis:// URL is not usable here — this store is REST.
#
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=https://your-db.upstash.io
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=your_token_here
#
# Older name for the same thing, from when Vercel KV provisioned it:
# KV_REST_API_URL=https://your-db.upstash.io
# KV_REST_API_TOKEN=your_token_here

# Reading receipts (optional). Without it the "From a receipt" mode is not
# offered at all and /api/nota/scan answers 503 — a bill is still built by
# typing the lines, or by splitting a total evenly.
#
# Server-only: this key is read in a route handler and never reaches the
# browser, which is why it has no NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix. Do not add one.
#
# The photo is sent to the model and dropped when the request ends — it is
# never written to disk, to the Redis above, or to a log. See
# src/lib/ai/scan.ts.
#
# The endpoint is rate-limited per caller and costs money per call. Keep the
# key off any deployment you don't want billed.
#
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# Pointing the scanner somewhere other than Anthropic (optional).
#
# A key issued by an Anthropic-compatible gateway is not an Anthropic key: left
# at the default it is sent to api.anthropic.com, which answers 401 and looks
# exactly like a wrong key. Set both of these together with such a key — the
# endpoint has to move with the credential, and a gateway names its models
# however it likes.
#
# Read docs/PRIVACY.md before setting these. It is not a routing change: the
# receipt photos then reach whoever operates that host, under their retention
# policy rather than Anthropic's, and the privacy page says as much to whoever
# is deciding whether to photograph their receipt.
#
# The SDK appends /v1/messages itself, so give the host — plus any prefix the
# gateway is mounted under — and no trailing /v1. One set anyway is dropped
# rather than sent on as /v1/v1/messages, which answers 404.
#
# ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=https://your-gateway.example

# Which header the credential travels in. Anthropic wants x-api-key, which is
# what ANTHROPIC_API_KEY above sends. Most gateways want the bearer
# convention instead — set ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN and the same string goes out
# as Authorization: Bearer. It wins if both are set. Sending the wrong one of
# the two answers 401 and reads exactly like a wrong key.
#
# ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN=
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-opus-4-8
